# Trivy ignore list for fulmen-toolbox runner / sbom-tools images.
#
# Add CVEs here only with rationale and a date. Format:
#   <CVE-ID>  # YYYY-MM-DD: <rationale>; review by YYYY-MM-DD
#
# This file is read by the cve-scan workflow and by `make precommit` (trivy
# scan of Dockerfile sources). Keep entries minimal and time-boxed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADMISSION RULE: an entry belongs here only if the fix is genuinely out of our
# reach — the fix exists in a dependency, but no upstream release of the tool we
# ship carries it yet, AND we are already on that tool's latest release.
# "We haven't gotten to it" is not a rationale; bump the pin instead.
#
# v0.5.8 (2026-10-10): Docker was not available in this pin-refresh environment,
# so waivers were re-evaluated from upstream go.mod of the new pins (syft
# v1.54.0, grype v0.120.0, trivy v0.75.0) rather than a rebuilt-image scan.
# Dropped trivy-only waivers that those go.mod files show as cleared, and
# dropped syft/grype Go-stdlib waivers whose fix line is older than the
# toolchain those releases require. Re-scan published images after GA and drop
# anything that no longer appears. Do not carry an entry forward on trust.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Go stdlib embedded in PREBUILT upstream binaries ------------------------
# yq v4.53.3 remains built with go1.26.4 (unchanged pin). syft v1.54.1 and
# grype v0.120.1 require go 1.26.8; trivy v0.75.0 requires go 1.27.0 — those
# carriers are past the go1.26.5 stdlib fix line. This leftover needs go1.26.5.
CVE-2026-39822  # 2026-10-10: stdlib in prebuilt yq v4.53.3 (go1.26.4); needs go1.26.5; yq pin unchanged; review by 2026-12-31

# --- golang.org/x/text in prebuilt / upstream-pinned binaries ----------------
# Two remaining carriers, neither of which we can move this cut:
#   golangci-lint v2.12.2 -> x/text v0.36.0. We DO build this from source, so
#     the version comes from its own go.mod, not our toolchain. Unchanged pin.
#   yq v4.53.3 (unchanged) -> x/text v0.37.0.
# trivy v0.75.0 now vendors x/text v0.42.0 (past the v0.39.0 fix) and is
# dropped from this waiver. Fixed in x/text v0.39.0; clears as each remaining
# upstream bumps its dependency.
CVE-2026-56852  # 2026-10-10: x/text in golangci-lint v2.12.2 (v0.36.0) and yq v4.53.3 (v0.37.0); fixed in v0.39.0; trivy v0.75.0 no longer a carrier; review by 2026-12-31

# --- Vendored dependencies in prebuilt upstream binaries ---------------------
# grype still vendors github.com/docker/docker v28.5.2 (fixed in v29.3.1).
# Re-checked 2026-10-14 against grype v0.120.1 go.mod — the dependency is
# unchanged, so the version bump taken this cycle did not clear it.
CVE-2026-34040  # 2026-10-14: grype v0.120.1 vendors docker/docker v28.5.2; fixed in 29.3.1; on-latest-upstream; review by 2026-12-31

# --- Bundled npm dependency tree --------------------------------------------
# We pin npm to 12.0.1 (see the npm stage in the goneat Dockerfiles), which
# cleared CRITICAL CVE-2026-59873 (tar) plus CVE-2026-59874, CVE-2026-48815
# (sigstore), CVE-2026-13149 (brace-expansion) and CVE-2026-33671 (picomatch).
# npm 12.0.1 bundles brace-expansion 5.0.7; this advisory needs 5.0.8, which no
# published npm release ships yet. Clears on the next npm that bundles it — at
# which point the pin bump closes this without further work.
CVE-2026-14257  # 2026-07-30: brace-expansion 5.0.7 bundled inside pinned npm 12.0.1; fixed in 5.0.8; no npm release ships 5.0.8 yet; goneat-tools images only; review by 2026-10-30
